<p>
	<strong>Skill key:</strong> <em>Beginner</em> = breadboard + USB power; <em>Intermediate</em> = mains-safe relay logic or multiple I2C
	sensors; <em>Advanced</em> = displays, voice or air-quality stacks. Each idea below links to a deeper guide where we have one — start with{' '}
	<a href={`${p}smart-home/esp32-esphome-temperature-sensor/`}>ESPHome temperature</a> for project 1.
</p>

<h2 id="beginner">Beginner (1–2 hours)</h2>

<h3>1. Room temperature (DHT22)</h3>
<p>
	ESP32 + DHT22 per room. Full walkthrough: <a href={`${p}smart-home/esp32-esphome-temperature-sensor/`}>ESPHome temperature sensor</a>.
</p>

<h3>2. Panic button</h3>
<p>GPIO button fires a Home Assistant event—alarm, notify, “all off” scene.</p>

<pre><code>{`binary_sensor:
  - platform: gpio
    pin: GPIO4
    name: "Panic button"
    on_press:
      - homeassistant.event:
          event: panic_button`}</code></pre>

<h3>3. Status LED (WS2812)</h3>
<p>RGB strip shows house state—green OK, red window open, blue away.</p>

<h2 id="intermediate">Intermediate (2–4 hours)</h2>

<h3>4. Local weather node</h3>
<p>BME280 (temp, humidity, pressure) + optional BH1750 light—automate blinds from lux.</p>

<h3>5. Four-channel relay</h3>
<p>
	Drive fan, pump or gate logic—<strong>not</strong> mains unless you know the electrical code; prefer certified in-wall relays for{' '}
	{c.mainsVoltage} loads.
</p>
<p>Off-the-shelf Wi-Fi relay alternative: Shelly 1 Gen4 (local integration in HA).</p>

<h3>6. mmWave presence (LD2410)</h3>
<p>Detects still occupants—better than PIR for desks and beds.</p>

<h2 id="advanced">Advanced (4–8 hours)</h2>

<h3>7. E-paper dashboard</h3>
<p>2.9″ e-paper shows temp and forecast without a bright always-on LCD.</p>

<h3>8. CO₂ (MH-Z19B or SCD4x)</h3>
<p>
	Alert and boost ventilation above ~1000 ppm. Pi + SCD41 MQTT path:{' '}
	<a href={`${p}smart-home/raspberry-pi-co2-scd41-home-assistant/`}>Raspberry Pi CO₂</a>.
</p>

<h3>9. Local voice (Atom Echo / HA Voice)</h3>
<p>Wake word and commands without Google/Alexa cloud—requires HA voice pipeline setup.</p>

<h3>10. Pulse counting</h3>
<p>Hall sensor on utility meter impulses—track water or (where legal) electricity pulses.</p>

<h2 id="bonus">Bonus ideas</h2>
<ul>
	<li><strong>ESP32-CAM + relay:</strong> gate or doorbell camera locally in HA</li>
	<li><strong>Soil moisture + valve:</strong> garden irrigation when dry</li>
	<li><strong>PIR + siren:</strong> DIY alarm entities in HA</li>
	<li><strong>BME680 + PMS5003:</strong> indoor air quality stack</li>
</ul>

