<h2 id="faq">FAQ</h2>

<h3>Do I need to code in C++?</h3>
<p><strong>ESPHome</strong> uses YAML; you flash from Home Assistant or the ESPHome CLI. Arduino C is optional for custom firmware.</p>

<h3>ESP32 or Zigbee?</h3>
<p>
	<strong>ESP32</strong> for USB-powered custom sensors; <strong>Zigbee</strong> for battery mesh nodes —{' '}
	<a href={`${p}smart-home/zigbee-temperature-sensor/`}>Zigbee temperature guide</a>.
</p>

<h3>Which board first?</h3>
<p>See <a href={`${p}smart-home/which-esp32-board-for-smart-home/`}>which ESP32 board for smart home</a>.</p>

<h3>Run Home Assistant on Pi 5?</h3>
<p>
	Yes — <strong>4GB</strong> is enough for HA plus a few add-ons: <a href={`${p}raspberry-pi-5-which-ram/`}>Pi 5 RAM guide</a>.
</p>